// endpoint_send_hidden_keepalives.proto — SendHiddenKeepalives: send one
// keep-alive to the session of every workspace in the HIDDEN WORKSPACES
// section. SIDEBAR section. Daemon-scoped: the request names no workspace,
// and Emacs calls it over its one daemon-level connection (`SPC j R`).
//
// A hidden workspace's keep-alives are HELD (SetWorkspaceHidden), so its
// prompt cache lapses on its own clock and its session is stood down when it
// does. This request asks each hidden workspace's shim for ONE keep-alive now
// (shim.v1.SendKeepalive), leaving every cadence held: the cache is
// re-anchored by the keep-alive's own request, each shim restates its
// projected lapse, and the hidden section's countdowns move later on the
// roster stream. Nothing in this answer carries a lapse; the roster does.
//
// THE DAEMON ASKS EVERY HIDDEN WORKSPACE AT ONCE, and answers when every one
// has answered, so one slow shim delays the answer but never another
// workspace's keep-alive.

